OBJECTIVES:

1. To develop a menu-driven Hospital Patient Management System for maintaining patient
records efficiently.
2. To store patient details such as patient ID, name, age, disease, and allotted bed number in
a doubly linked list.
3. To perform essential operations such as admitting new patients, searching for patient
records, discharging patients, and displaying records.
4. To display patient information in both forward and backward directions using the doubly
linked list.
5. To use an array for managing hospital bed allocation and helping track available beds.
6. To use a stack to store discharged patient details and support undoing the most recent
discharge.
7. To apply dynamic memory allocation and linked-list operations for flexible record
management.
8. To improve accuracy, accessibility, and organization of patient information while reducing
manual record-handling effort.